# GENASIS.md — agentic team protocol contract

> Generated by `genasis` v{{ genasis_version | default(value="0.0.1") }}.
> Edits inside marker fences are tracked by hash; edits outside are preserved.
> Re-run `genasis upgrade` to bump the contract.

## Project
- **name**: `{{ project_name }}`
- **domain**: `{{ project_domain }}`
- **Plane**: `{{ plane_url }}` (flavor: `{{ plane_flavor | default(value="auto") }}`)
- **Mattermost**: `{{ mm_url }}` (flavor: `{{ mm_flavor | default(value="auto") }}`)

## Lifecycle
- 1 Plane issue = 1 Mattermost thread = 1 git branch.
- Owner = the agent whose UUID appears in `assignees`.
- State transitions are owned by the assignee (PM does not transition on behalf).
- Read [`docs/agent-ownership.md`](docs/agent-ownership.md) for the full state machine.

## Communication
- All human ↔ team communication goes through Mattermost `#scrum-{{ project_name }}` (threaded per issue) and Plane (state, comments).
- Direct CLI by humans is reserved for bridge outages.

## Design system
- Single source of truth: `docs/design-system.md`.
- Hot-swappable via `genasis design swap <reference-url>`.
- Frontend agents must reference `design-system.md` before introducing tokens / colors / layouts.

## Database
- Read: `genasis db query "SELECT ..."` (DDL/DML rejected by lex guard).
- Write: `genasis db migrate` (Atlas / Drizzle Kit / DuckDB raw runner — auto-detected).

## Token economics
- RTK is auto-registered when present.
- Stable prefix in this file is intentional — do not reorder sections without bumping `genasis upgrade`.
